{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/eventmacros\/event(name:consent:version:)"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Makes a struct an event: derives its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformances, its name and its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" from its declaration.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@attached"},{"kind":"text","text":"(extension, conformances: "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events5EventP","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","text":"Event"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SE","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Encodable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Se","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Decodable"},{"kind":"text","text":", names: named(name), named(consentCategory), named(schemaVersion), named(schema), named(constraintViolation), named(CodingKeys), named(encode(to:)), named(init(from:)), named(decodeValue), named(decodeIfPresentValue), named(requireCodable), named(codableRequirements), named(__discoveryRecord)) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Event"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"name"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"consent"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events15ConsentCategoryV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","text":"ConsentCategory"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"version"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1)"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"name","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The name destinations record the event under, a string literal; the type’s name when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"name":"consent","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The purpose the event is collected for; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"name":"version","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The schema version, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event.schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a positive integer literal, raised for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each breaking change; 1 by default.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import EventMacros","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\", consent: .functional, version: 2)","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int?","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The macro adds an extension holding:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"static var name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when ","type":"text"},{"code":"name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is given; otherwise the type’s name, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s default.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static var consentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":", when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consent"},{"type":"text","text":" is given; otherwise "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"static var schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when ","type":"text"},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is given; otherwise 1, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"static var schema","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" with the event’s name, version and each stored","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property’s name, type as written, optionality, whether it has a default value and validation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keywords (its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" type’s rule’s, then those ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Constrained(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" declares), in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration order. A property of a raw-value enum gets its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema\/Enumeration","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", the cases’ raw values. The macro lists them when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enum is declared inside the struct, and reads them from ","type":"text"},{"code":"allCases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for one declared elsewhere","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or with a case under ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". An enum declared elsewhere needs ","type":"text"},{"code":"CaseIterable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a tracking","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan to check its values; without it, and for a typealias of an enum, the plan accepts any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"constraintViolation()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when a property declares constraints with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Constrained(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first property, in declaration order, whose value breaks one, which a tracker rejects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"CodingKeys","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"encode(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the private functions it reads some types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through, which write a keyed container of the stored","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties, each under its name, and read each back by its name, as a hand-written","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conformance would. A store writes the container as a CBOR map. An optional property’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is left out, and an optional property missing from the map reads as ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; one with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default value reads as that value, so its ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is written. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, optional or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not, and each date in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date?]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, is written as the seconds since 2001","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it stores, so it reads back exactly. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type of your own takes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"CBOR package’s own form, seconds since 1970, and reads back to within a rounding of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"microsecond’s scale. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"text":" property goes through its own conformance, so only a store writes its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A second extension holds a private "},{"code":"__discoveryRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which the compiler places in the binary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the event at run time, and "},{"code":"SegmentStore()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"DatabaseStore(database:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"TrackingPlan()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" take it without a list. A generic struct, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one nested in a generic type’s declaration, gets no record, as a generic type can’t hold a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"static stored property: it isn’t discovered, and the macro adds a note saying to list it. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct declared in an extension of a generic type doesn’t compile ("},{"code":"static stored properties not supported in generic types","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), as the extension doesn’t say the type is generic; declare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it outside the generic type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every stored instance property is encoded, and needs a type annotation. Static and computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties are left out, and so is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"let","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with an initial value, which every value shares.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The struct keeps its memberwise initializer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A stored property whose type isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" is a compile error naming it:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static method 'requireCodable(bad:)' requires that 'Foo' conform to 'Decodable'"},{"type":"text","text":" for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bad"},{"type":"text","text":" of type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Foo"},{"type":"text","text":". A raw-value enum is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":", written as its raw value, once it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declares the conformance ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"enum Reason: String, Codable"},{"type":"text","text":"). One declared inside the struct must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list it in its inheritance clause, even when an extension adds it, since the macro sees only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the struct; without it, the error is the macro’s own, at that clause. Applying the macro to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anything but a struct, a property with no type annotation, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lazy"},{"type":"text","text":" property, a destructuring"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pattern, a name that isn’t a non-empty string literal and a version that isn’t a positive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integer literal are compile errors too."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Changing-an-event","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Changing an event"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store may still hold records written before an event’s stored properties changed: an app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"updates with records on disk it hasn’t delivered. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" counts the changes those records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can’t be read through, and only those. Each record carries the version it was stored at, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store drops one stored at another version than the type’s now without reading it, reporting the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event and both versions ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DropReport.versionMismatch"},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracking plan’s check"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":") fails on a change that needs a new version while the version stayed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same, naming the event, the property and the change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These changes are compatible. Keep the version, and the records stored before the change are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read by each property’s name, in any order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Version 1, as released.","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\")","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var screen: String","}","","\/\/ Still version 1: a record stored above reads with coupon nil, currency \"USD\" and screen","\/\/ skipped.","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\")","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var coupon: String?          \/\/ an optional property added: nil","    var currency: String = \"USD\" \/\/ a property with a default value added: the default","                                 \/\/ screen removed: its stored value is skipped","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These changes are breaking. Raise the version with each, and the records stored at the earlier","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one are dropped and reported:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@Event(name: \"checkout_started\", version: 2)","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Double  \/\/ a property's type changed (it was Int)","    var coupon: String    \/\/ an optional property made required (it was String?)","    var paymentMethod: String \/\/ a required property added, with no default value","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A version raised for a change whose bytes would still read, such as a property that keeps its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type but changes its meaning, drops the earlier records all the same, so they are never read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the new shape. Records are never migrated from one version to another.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:11EventMacros0A04name7consent7versionySSSg_6Events15ConsentCategoryVSgSitcfm","roleHeading":"Macro","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/EventMacros\/Event.swift#L132","fileName":"Event.swift"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Event"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"name"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"consent"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events15ConsentCategoryV","text":"ConsentCategory"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"version"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"symbolKind":"macro","modules":[{"name":"EventMacros"}],"title":"Event(name:consent:version:)"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Event(name:consent:version:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Events/documentation/Events/Sensitive":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Sensitive","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A property value that a destination reads only through the record it arrived in, and not at all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once the record is redacted."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sensitive","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"topic","title":"Sensitive","url":"\/documentation\/events\/sensitive"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros/Constrained(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Declares the constraints a stored property of an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" struct satisfies, which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checks an